; spell.self — the SELF cluster: rewrite yourself, verify, roll back.
; STATUS: contract stub. Blocked by the hotswap API (programmatic
; compile-string→binary + :code.load_binary exposed to the language)
; and by BOUNDARY (reading ns forms as data for the dependency walk).
;
; The thesis cluster — the reason the harness exists. First principles
; changes WHAT THE ARTIFACT OF TRUST IS at each step (see README):
;
;   jank:   snapshot SOURCE → re-eval to restore → revert can fail to
;           compile against a changed sibling (:revert-error — "instead
;           of claiming a recovery it did not perform")
;   here:   snapshot BINARY → :code.load_binary to restore → a binary
;           cannot fail to compile; it already did. The failure mode
;           is not handled; it ceases to exist.
;
; ── Contract ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; (save! ns-sym source) → {:saved beam-binary} | {:error msg}
;   Compile source for ns-sym to a .beam binary WITHOUT loading it.
;   The candidate exists as a binary first — an artifact that can be
;   hashed, diffed, and remembered — before it can affect anything.
;
; (swap! ns-sym source verify-fn) →
;     {:swapped :verified} | {:swapped :reverted :error msg} | {:error msg}
;   The one operation the harness needs:
;     1. save! the candidate binary
;     2. remember the currently-loaded binary for ns-sym's module
;     3. :code.load_binary the candidate
;     4. (spell.fence/fence verify-fn [] probe-timeout) — the probe
;        (render a known state; jank called this verify-render)
;     5. probe ok → commit: remember candidate as the new known-good
;        probe fails/timeout → revert: load_binary the REMEMBERED BINARY
;   Revert is total: it cannot fail for the reason jank's could.
;
; (dep-order ns-sym) → {:order [ns…]} | {:error :cycle [ns…]}
;   Pure fn over ns FORMS (data, via BOUNDARY's reader — no string
;   scanning like jank's spell_scan_deps). swap! walks this order when
;   a change crosses namespaces.
;
; Rescue keys (ctrl+r = swap! from disk, ctrl+z = revert to known-good)
; are NOT here and NOT in the event handler: they belong to the
; renderer's OWNER process (main.bl), which sees events before the
; possibly-broken handler — jank's pump-convention invariant, enforced
; by supervision structure instead of code order.
;
; Known-good snapshots live in STORE: (state-ensure :known-good {}) —
; a named cell mapping ns-sym → beam binary, so the snapshot survives
; the very reload it protects against.

(ns spell.self)
